\label{thm:main}
Let $G$ be a strongly connected signed digraph on $[n]$ without positive cycles. Either
\begin{itemize}
\item $G$ is a cycle and no BN on $G$ is synchronizing, or
\item every and-or-net on $G$ has a synchronizing word of length at most $10(\sqrt{5}+1)^n$.
\end{itemize}

