\label{pro:BN_switch}
If $h$ is the $I$-switch of $f$, then:
\begin{itemize}
\item the signed interaction digraph of $h$ is the $I$-switch of the signed interaction digraph of $f$;
\item if $f$ is an and-or-net, then $h$ is an and-or-net;
\item for any word $w$, $h^w$ is the $I$-switch of $f^w$.
\end{itemize}

